.TH DARPA-SPILL-BACKFILL 1 "September 24, 2026" "darpa_spillserver 1.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
darpa-spill-backfill \- fill the spill archive from a TDU's ring buffer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B darpa-spill-backfill
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The ingest poller in
.BR darpa-spill-server (1)
only moves forward. Its
.B ingest.backfill
setting applies on a cold start and nowhere else, so once a source has any
rows the poller never reaches back past them. Whatever the TDU already held
before the server was first pointed at it \(em on a ring holding thirty hours,
most of the data \(em would otherwise never be archived.
.PP
.B darpa-spill-backfill
walks a time range in windows, asking each configured TDU's
.I /spill_history
route for one window at a time and inserting what comes back.
.SS Why windows
.I /spill_history
applies its
.B limit
after collecting everything at or after
.BR since ,
so a wide request with a small limit still makes the TDU produce the whole
remainder of the ring. Bounding both ends keeps each request proportional to
its window. When a window returns more rows than
.B \-\-limit
allows, it is halved (down to one second) and the same stretch is re-read,
so no events are skipped silently.
.SS Finding the start of the ring
Without
.BR \-\-start ,
the tool probes backwards from
.B \-\-end
in doubling strides from one hour (up to 30 days) until a one-minute window
comes back empty, then binary-searches that bracket to within five minutes.
The ring can span more than the current TCRMonitor run: that process resets
its event counter on start but does not clear the segment, so older runs'
events survive past the insert point. Their timestamps are genuine; only the
.B event_number
sequence restarts, so it is not continuous across that boundary.
.SS Safety
Inserts are idempotent, keyed on
.RI ( nova_time ", " spill_type ", " signal_code ),
so re-running over a range already archived costs time and changes nothing.
It is safe to run while the server is ingesting: the archive is in SQLite WAL
mode and the two writers do not block each other. A source whose TDU has no
bulk history route is reported and skipped.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fIFILE\fR
YAML configuration file, as for
.BR darpa-spill-server (1).
It supplies the sources, TDU timeouts and archive path.
.TP
.BI \-\-env\-file " FILE"
Read \fBDARPA_SPILL_\fR variables from this \fB.env\fR file. Without it,
\fB$DARPA_SPILL_ENV_FILE\fR names the file, else
.I ./.env
is read if it exists.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-database " " \fIFILE\fR
Archive to write into; overrides the configuration.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-source " " \fINAME\fR
Only backfill this configured source. May be repeated. Default: every
configured source.
.TP
.BI \-\-start " TIME"
Start of the range. Default: the earliest time the TDU still holds, found by
probing.
.TP
.BI \-\-end " TIME"
End of the range. Default \fBnow\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-window " SECONDS"
Seconds of TDU time requested per call. Default \fB300\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-limit " N"
Maximum rows per request. Default \fB20000\fR.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Report the range and how many windows would be requested, without fetching
or writing.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Print only the per-source and final summaries, and log only warnings.
.PP
Write relative times with an equals sign \(em
.BR \-\-start=\-6h ,
not
.B \-\-start \-6h
\(em or the option parser takes the value for an option.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Settings merge in the server's order: command line > environment > .env >
YAML file > defaults. See
.BR darpa-spill-server (1).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DARPA_SPILL_CONFIG
Configuration file, as \fB\-\-config\fR.
.TP
.B DARPA_SPILL_ENV_FILE
\&.env file, as \fB\-\-env\-file\fR.
.TP
.BI DARPA_SPILL_ SECTION _ KEY
Overrides any single setting, e.g.
.BR DARPA_SPILL_TDU_HISTORY_TIMEOUT .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Finished; every reachable source was walked, or skipped with a message.
.TP
.B 1
Interrupted. Rows already inserted are kept.
.TP
.B 2
A configuration error, an unknown \fB\-\-source\fR, or a malformed time.
.SH EXAMPLES
See how much the TDUs still hold, without writing anything:
.PP
.RS
.EX
darpa\-spill\-backfill \-c config/spillserver.yaml \-\-dry\-run
.EE
.RE
.PP
Fill everything the ring holds for one source:
.PP
.RS
.EX
darpa\-spill\-backfill \-c config/spillserver.yaml \-s tdu\-near\-master\-ppc\-01
.EE
.RE
.PP
Fill the last six hours, in smaller windows, into another archive:
.PP
.RS
.EX
darpa\-spill\-backfill \-\-start=\-6h \-\-window 60 \-d /var/lib/darpa\-spillserver/spills.db
.EE
.RE
